        "listen": {
          "explanationKey": "The Nation’s first motto was “E Pluribus Unum.” What does that mean?",
          "facts": [
            "The nation's first motto was “E Pluribus Unum.” It means “Out of many, one.”",
            "Say it like this: ee PLOOR-ih-bus OO-num.",
            "It says that many people and many states become one country.",
            "The national anthem is “The Star-Spangled Banner.” It is a song about the American flag."
          ],
          "newWords": [
            {
              "word": "motto",
              "meaning": "a short saying that tells what a group believes"
            },
            {
              "word": "anthem",
              "meaning": "a country's official song"
            }
          ]
        },
